 "result_text": "`DefFrame` now supports `CHANNEL-DELAY`.\n\nI checked it with one quick parse-and-print of a `DEFFRAME` that sets `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-7`. The attribute parsed into the new `channel_delay` field and printed back out (as `1e-07`). I didn't run the test suite or add tests.\n\n- **`DefFrame` object:** `pyquil/quilbase.py` has a new optional `channel_delay: Optional[float]` field. It is written out as `CHANNEL-DELAY` in `out()`, and the keyword is added to the reserved-keyword list.\n- **Parsing:** `CHANNEL-DELAY` is added to the frame attributes in `pyquil/_parser/grammar.lark` and mapped to `channel_delay` in `pyquil/_parser/parser.py`.\n\nI did not add a separate `CHANNELDELAY` terminal to the grammar's analog-keyword list. The attribute works without it.",
